# DEVELOPMENT SIGNING
#
# This is an output template for `just signing-configure`. Do not copy
# the placeholder values into `.env.dev`.
#
# Required access:
# - A member of the Apple Developer Program team that owns the explicit App IDs
#   `com.openjoystickdriver` and `com.openjoystickdriver.XboxUSBDevice`, with
#   an Account Holder or Admin available to create the profiles.
# - The team's Account Holder must first obtain Apple's required managed HID and
#   DriverKit entitlements. A different team cannot create profiles for these
#   globally owned identifiers.
#
# Before running `signing configure`:
# 1. Create an Apple Development certificate with its private key in the login
#    keychain. Create it in Xcode > Settings > Accounts > Manage Certificates.
# 2. A Mac App Development profile for `com.openjoystickdriver`, downloaded as
#    `~/Documents/Profiles/OpenJoystickDriver.provisionprofile`.
# 3. A DriverKit Development profile for
#    `com.openjoystickdriver.XboxUSBDevice`, downloaded as
#    `~/Documents/Profiles/OpenJoystickDriver_XboxUSBDevice.provisionprofile`.
#    It needs only the DriverKit and `transport.usb` entitlements, with Apple's
#    exact seven-device grant for vendor ID 1118. It must not carry the HID
#    entitlements or `com.apple.developer.hid.virtual.device`; the app profile
#    carries `hid.virtual.device` for IOHIDUserDevice.
#
# See docs/development/signing.md for the portal capabilities and profile steps.
#
# Unsigned local work (`swift build`, `just driverkit-check`) does not
# need this file. Signed development installs (`just install-dev`)
# do. Notarization credentials are not used here; they live in `.env.release`
# under the same names GitHub Actions injects, and cannot be read back from
# repository secrets.
#
# Then run:
#   just signing-install-profiles
#   just signing-configure
#
# `signing configure` replaces these values with the profiles' Team ID and
# paths and the SHA-1 of the Keychain identity that both profiles embed. That
# one identity signs the app and the DEXT; the build reads the DEXT's Xcode
# profile specifier from the Name inside DEXT_PROVISIONING_PROFILE. Any other
# key stops every repository script.
CODESIGN_IDENTITY="APPLE_DEVELOPMENT_CERTIFICATE_SHA1"
DEVELOPMENT_TEAM="YOUR_10_CHARACTER_TEAM_ID"
GUI_PROVISIONING_PROFILE="$HOME/Library/MobileDevice/Provisioning Profiles/OpenJoystickDriver.provisionprofile"
DEXT_PROVISIONING_PROFILE="$HOME/Library/MobileDevice/Provisioning Profiles/OpenJoystickDriver_XboxUSBDevice.provisionprofile"

# 1 uses the sibling ../SwifterKit checkout when it exists; unset uses the pinned remote.
# OJD_USE_LOCAL_SWIFTERKIT="1"
